es of travelogue, poetry, fiction, film, opera, photograph, painting, illustration, etc., the course critically examines the Orientalist dichotomy between the West and the non-West and analyzes the internalization of Orientalism in East Asia in constructing the marginalized other. In addition, through a combination of reading, writing, and in-class discussion, the course investigates the historical conditions surrounding the production and dissemination of Orientalist representations of East Asia and their relevance in the contemporary world. (SC)", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2025SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 351007, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "AAS", "catalogNbr": "4950", "titleShort": "Independent Study", "titleLong": "Independent Study", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "EUAREA", "descr": "European Studies Area", "descrformal": "European Studies Area", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies", "attrDescrShort": "ExplStudy"}, {"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "SAAREA", "descr": "South Asia Studies Area", "descrformal": "South Asia Studies Area", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies", "attrDescrShort": "ExplStudy"}, {"crseAttr": "0013", "crseAttrValue": "CU-UGR", "descr": "Undergraduate Research", "descrformal": "Undergraduate Research", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies",